From 75c3f73a6db767b2f764bb739a421c1a0b5bf479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:37:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci: mini state lane skips same-PR repeats and
 unrelated .github edits

The one mini runner (mini-hermes-state-1) ran at 0.88 utilisation on PR
`tests/hermes_state (macOS, mini)` jobs alone after #1912 dropped the
main-push runs: 08:23-16:00Z on 2026-11-13, 31 PR jobs started (~10.5 min
median, 368 runner-minutes), wait median 19.7 min, p90 63 min, max 91 min.

Five whys
1. Why did PRs wait? Demand on the one runner was ~4 jobs/h at ~10 min.
2. Why that much demand? Branches re-ran the lane on every push: 9 of the
   31 started runs repeated their branch's previous passing run on identical
   content of every lane-routing file (e.g. wt/e6cce5965c-watch-mark 5 runs,
   hermes_state_outcome.py unchanged; wt/gateway-quiet-v3 4 runs, pyproject.toml
   unchanged). 3 more were PRs whose only lane trigger was an unrelated
   `.github/` edit (ci-review-comment.yml, actions/fetch-merge-base).
3. Why did those run the lane? classify_changes forced hermes_state on any
   `.github/` change, and nothing remembered that a PR had already passed.
4. Why does a `.github/` edit not need it? The lane runs no local action: only
   hermes-state-macos.yml and its caller ci.yaml change what runs on the mini.
5. Why can a repeat be skipped? The routing contract already leaves surface
   files a PR does not change to their own PRs and the 4-hourly main schedule;
   a repeat that changes none of the routing files' content adds nothing.

Change
- classify_changes: under `.github/`, only HERMES_STATE_WIRING (the lane
  workflow and ci.yaml) routes hermes_state, like native_memory's exact-path
  rule. Empty diffs, capped lists and CI-config files (justfile,
  scripts/hermes-python) still run it.
- scripts/ci/macos_state_reuse.py keys a same-repository PR's lane by the git
  tree entries, at the PR merge commit, of every changed file that routes the
  lane plus the lane workflow. detect looks it up (actions/cache restore,
  lookup-only); a hit turns hermes_state off for that PR run only. macOS state
  required (v1) saves the key after a pass in this run. Every failure (no key,
  lookup error, save error) means the lane runs; fork PRs, releases, dispatch
  and pushes never reuse. A reused lane is "not selected", which the required
  check already accepts.

Not changed, with evidence
- Superseded same-PR runs: all 7 cancelled lane jobs in the window were
  cancelled before they started (CI's per-PR group, cancel-in-progress).
- Duration creep (14-19 min at 14:09-15:50Z): the same suite took 9.2 min at
  15:40Z between 17.3 and 17.2 min runs; the mini's 15-min load average was 34
  (operator sample 15:50Z) with 8 hermes-sync-macos runs queued: host contention,
  not test growth.
- A second runner on the mini: ruled out (BB host load and memory pressure).

Replay of the window: removing the 9 repeats and 3 .github-only runs takes
~120 of 368 runner-minutes (33%) off the lane.

Tests: tests/ci/test_macos_state_reuse.py (new: key, gate replay, step
conditions, lookup/save pairing, no local action in the lane);
tests/ci/test_classify_changes.py (.github cases).
Card: t_01a1d58663f79436.
